 "publicacion": {
  "titulo": "For every $1 on defense, America pays $1.08 in interest",
  "descripcion": "US federal interest payments ran at a $1.33 trillion annual rate in Q3 2026, against $1.23 trillion for national defense: $1.08 for every defense dollar, up from 62 cents in early 2020. The Fed's rate went from 0.08% to 5.33% between Dec 2021 and Aug 2023. Interest passed defense in Q1 2024 and has stayed above for 11 quarters (it also did for one quarter, Q1 1998). The money goes to bondholders, and interest does not reduce the debt. Gross interest; defense = consumption + gross investment. Ratios are our own calculation from BEA data via FRED. Not financial advice. #shorts #economy #nationaldebt #interestrates #money"
 },
